Think about how different developer
use an open source library.

150
00:10:33,756 --> 00:10:40,277
One Android app ships a full or PyTorch,
ExecuTorch Android native runtime.

151
00:10:40,619 --> 00:10:44,719
Another developer imports an Noctua AI
just for the heuristic, and omits the

152
00:10:44,725 --> 00:10:47,276
native dependency to keep their APK tiny.

153
00:10:48,027 --> 00:10:53,332
And our own CI server run unit test on
a standard desktop JVM, where Android

154
00:10:53,354 --> 00:10:59,270
JNI library doesn't exist If our SDK
hard-coded a direct dependency on the

155
00:10:59,270 --> 00:11:04,564
runtime C++ runtime, unit test and
lightweight consumer could immediately

156
00:11:04,565 --> 00:11:06,827
crash on unsatisfied link error.

157
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:11,234
So in Noctua, we build a
defensive dual path forecaster.

158
00:11:11,453 --> 00:11:14,270
Our primary path is ExecuTorch forecaster.

159
00:11:14,629 --> 00:11:19,050
It loads an ExecuTorch native
runtime reflectively at runtime

160
00:11:19,075 --> 00:11:23,279
