161
00:11:23,865 --> 00:11:27,796
When it runs, UI explicitly
displays a neural ExecuTorch

162
00:11:27,825 --> 00:11:31,649
telemetry batch, so the known neural
engine produce the prediction.

163
00:11:32,406 --> 00:11:35,022
Our fallback is Linear
Heuristic Forecaster.

164
00:11:35,285 --> 00:11:40,943
If the native runtime PTE file is missing
for any reason, Noctua catches cleanly

165
00:11:40,969 --> 00:11:42,983
and fall back to the zero dependency.

166
00:11:43,443 --> 00:11:47,839
Pure Kotlin linear model updating
the UI batches to linear fallback.

167
00:11:48,149 --> 00:11:52,971
Because of this pattern, all
sixteen unit test cases can cleanly

168
00:11:53,774 --> 00:11:57,742
run on a standard JVM, and the
app never breaks in production

169
00:11:58,742 --> 00:12:02,498
From a developer experience standpoint,
